        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Hi Karen, it's Joe. I'm calling about Dad's birthday party on Saturday. First, the plan has changed a little. We're now having the party at my house, not at the restaurant, because the restaurant is closed for repairs. It starts at five o'clock instead of six, so please come a bit earlier if you can. Can you bring a cake? Mum is making the main food: roast chicken and salad. Uncle Peter is bringing drinks, and my wife is organising the music. Dad doesn't know about the party, so please don't tell him. I told him we're only having a family dinner. Aunt Lucy is bringing him in her car at half past five. We're going to hide in the living room and shout Surprise when he walks in. Oh, and parking is difficult near my house, so I suggest you take the bus. The number twenty-two stops on my street. It's about ten minutes from the stop to the house, and you can't miss the blue door. Call me back if you have any questions. Bye for now!"
      }
